# Suppressions for the bootstrap stack. Every line needs a reason.
#
# AWS-0089 — "Bucket has logging disabled" (LOW)
#   Literally true: S3 server access logging is off, and stays off.
#
#   It cannot be pointed at the log archive. S3 requires a server access
#   logging target bucket to be owned by the same account as the source, and
#   the archive is deliberately in a different account. Logging into a bucket
#   in the same account as the thing being audited defeats the purpose.
#
#   Access to this bucket is instead recorded as CloudTrail S3 **data events**,
#   scoped to exactly this bucket in modules/logging, and delivered to the
#   object-locked archive in awlz-log-archive. That is a stronger control than
#   the one the check is asking for.
#
#   Threat model: T6b, closed.
AWS-0089
